Single-database configuration for Flask (Flask-Migrate / Alembic).

    flask db upgrade             # apply all migrations
    flask db migrate -m "..."    # autogenerate a new revision (review it!)
    flask db downgrade -1        # roll back one revision

Every revision must:

* run on both PostgreSQL and SQLite (use op.batch_alter_table for ALTERs);
* name every constraint explicitly (see NAMING_CONVENTION in ledgerline/extensions.py);
* provide a working downgrade();
* leave the database matching the models (tests/migrations/test_migrations.py checks this).
